  "notes": [
    "Shipped, machine-independent baseline (E7). Levels come only from the --help captures under references/cli/help (verified, with evidence.help_capture and evidence.help_version) or from vendor documentation (documented, evidence.docs); nothing in this file comes from a probe on any machine, so a live probe result (for example codex image generation) stays documented here and becomes verified only in that machine's overlay.",
    "Machine-specific blockers (auth_tier, quota, zdr, missing_flag, probe_failed, reprobe) never appear here: probes write them to ~/.momm/capabilities-<machine>.json. The one structural blocker recorded is antigravity's headless run_command allowlist, which every fresh install lacks.",
    "Input cell `how` and `requires` are binding templates: `{file}` is repeated per staged artefact, `{dir}` is the step's private work directory; a template that starts with `-` is bound into argv, otherwise the token containing {file} is written into the prompt. Text after `(` is description only.",
    "Input modalities: text, image, pdf, audio, video, speech (live microphone). Output modalities: text, image_gen, video_gen, speech (TTS), code_exec, web. Docs URLs are those listed in references/cli/modalities.md."
  ],
